•fauthorxApub:sha2-256:xytkvt7dua7tvt6vydqu22rlr53vttuxh77sholft4p7sx4qrqjqdbodyßeclassharchivalgcontentxurecipe-host 0.1.3 was released on 2026-10-22 from commit affd60308a3e0ba6cc803672e05178189ffc9f7f with these changes.ddata¢gcolumnsÇ°dnamehcategory°dnamefchangedrowsäÇhinternalx^npm test writes an LCOV coverage report, which CI gives SonarQube Cloud for its coverage gate.ÇeaddedxêA home page of the reader's favourite recipes, starred on the recipe list or a recipe's page and kept in the browser for each recipe repository.ÇeaddedxªThe recipe list moves from #/ to #/recipes and works like the ingredient list, with filter chips for each category and for breakfast, lunch and dinner tags; #/ is now the favourites page.Çeaddedx[A logo and browser-tab icon: the Sustenaut disc with a steaming pot in place of the sprout.ÇefixedxÜHeader links not selected are muted brown instead of Pure CSS grey, and a visited selected link is no longer black on the dark header.Çhinternalx¶The browser tests record which lines of app/app.js they run, and CI runs them in the test job so SonarQube Cloud counts that coverage; test/ is analysed as test code.ÇeaddedxÚSign-in for readers: a login section in recipe-host.yml (an OpenID Connect issuer and client, and whether reading needs it) signs readers in with the code flow and PKCE, coming back to the same view and ?repo=. Sites without it are unchanged.ÇeaddedxˇFavourites in the signed-in reader's own bucket: favourites in recipe-host.yml names a service that hands out short-lived links to one file per repository, so they follow the reader between browsers. What the browser kept moves there at the first sign-in.Çeaddedx¢recipe-host serve --mock-login previews a site with a local stand-in for the Sustenaut sign-in and favourites service, with test accounts and an in-memory bucket.ÇefixedxUThe logo's pot has no lid line, so the mark reads as a pot and steam without clutter.gdependsÅxApub:sha2-256:ydol4w44h234eqriouurmx2garpsg624kvgu6itu3h64b4zv